          "text": "The compile passed. But let me verify the semantics against the tests.\n\nTest T1: step 0 dt=0, DO_LOW false -> permit false, timer resets, run false, count 0. OK.\nStep1: DO_LOW true, dt=100. TON with IN true and dt... The TON depends on invocation timing. However, the harness likely uses dt_ms as real elapsed time between invocations. TON accumulates elapsed. At step1 elapsed 100ms. Step2 dt=4999 -> elapsed 5099? Wait that would be 100+4999=5099 >= 5000, but expected BLOWER_RUN false at step2! Hmm.\n\nWait step2 expected false with cumulative 5099ms. That contradicts. Unless timer zero at first eligible invocation: at step1 permit first true, elapsed=0 (first eligible invocation, elapsed zero). Then step2 dt 4999 -> elapsed 4999 <5000 -> false. Step3 dt=1 -> 5000 -> true. Yes matches: \"Timer elapsed time is zero on the first eligible sampled invocation\".\n\nTON in CODESYS: when IN becomes TRUE, timer starts with ET=0 at that call, then accumulates based on real time between calls. So at step1 (first TRUE) ET=0. Step2 adds 4999 -> 4999. Step3 adds 1 -> 5000, Q true. Good matches.\n\nT1 step5: DO_LOW false -> permit false -> TON reset IN false, run false. Step6: DO_LOW true dt=100 -> TON IN true first eligible, ET=0. Step7 dt=5000 -> 5000 Q true -> run true count 2. Matches expected.\n\nT2: step0 dt=0 DO_LOW true permit true -> first eligible ET=0, run false. Step1 dt=4000 -> ET=4000 false. Step2 E_STOP false -> permit false, reset. Step3 permit true dt=100 -> ET=0. Step4 dt=4999 -> 4999 false. Step5 dt=1 -> 5000 true run count1. Step6 E_STOP false -> run false count1. Matches.\n\nHowever, does TON reset properly when IN false then true? Yes.\n\nBut there's subtlety: does the harness use real time? The dt_ms is wall time presumably controlled. Fine.\n\nOne concern: count increments same invocation where run becomes true. bRunPrev initialized false, run true -> increment. Good.\n\nHowever at power-up BLOWER_RUN false and count 0 - VAR defaults. Good.\n\nCompilation passed. Provide final answer.\n\nBut wait—TON reset when E_STOP active: with IN false, ET=0. Good.\n\nEverything fine. Final answer."
